From 6ffa0e2ac6aaca5ffe47bb6ea6dbcf88f4cac590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom <tom@getimpala.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:11:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] restore: premap-hugepage: keep the target's 2 MiB phase
 so mremap keeps huge PMDs

Aligning the premapped VMA to a 2 MiB boundary is not enough: the PIE
restorer moves it to vma->e->start with mremap(), and move_page_tables()
only moves a huge PMD when old and new addresses are PMD-aligned at the
same point; otherwise it splits the PMD back to base pages. Measured on
an 8xB300 vLLM TP=2 image: the restore task held 237.8 GB of a 239.9 GB
worker in THP during population, and 143 MB after the mremap. Place the
premapped VMA at an address congruent to its target modulo 2 MiB instead;
the bump stays below one huge page so the existing reserve slack covers it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5.1
---
 criu/mem.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/criu/mem.c b/criu/mem.c
index 3d383d4e9..1da37a573 100644
--- a/criu/mem.c
+++ b/criu/mem.c
@@ -981,8 +981,22 @@ static int premap_private_vma(struct pstree_item *t, struct vma_area *vma, void
 		if (opts.premap_hugepage && size >= PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE &&
 		    !(vma->e->flags & MAP_HUGETLB) && !vma_area_is(vma, VMA_FILE_PRIVATE) &&
 		    !(vma->e->prot == PROT_NONE && vma_area_is(vma, VMA_AREA_NOT_ACCOUNTABLE))) {
-			*tgt_addr = (void *)(((unsigned long)*tgt_addr + PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE - 1) &
-					     ~(PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE - 1));
+			/*
+			 * Keep the target's 2 MiB phase, not a bare 2 MiB
+			 * alignment: the PIE restorer mremap()s the premapped
+			 * VMA to vma->e->start, and the kernel only moves a
+			 * huge PMD intact when the old and new addresses are
+			 * both PMD-aligned at that point. With equal phase the
+			 * whole aligned interior survives the move; with a
+			 * mismatch every PMD is split back to base pages.
+			 */
+			unsigned long phase = vma->e->start & (PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE - 1);
+			unsigned long cur = (unsigned long)*tgt_addr;
+			unsigned long cand = (cur & ~(PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE - 1)) + phase;
+
+			if (cand < cur)
+				cand += PREMAP_HPAGE_SIZE;
+			*tgt_addr = (void *)cand;
 			want_thp = true;
 		}
 
